governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different changes to the output, and each one would be tested differently. I need to know which one is wanted before I can write a contract for it.)
governor asks: What would make the output easier to read for you? Right now `todo list` shows lines like "[ ] buy milk" and "[x] walk dog". It doesn't show the id you need for `todo complete` or any due dates. Which of these do you want? (pick any)
(a) Show each todo's id, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk"
(b) Show due dates, e.g. "#1 [ ] buy milk (due 2026-11-01)"
(c) Line up ids, titles and due dates in columns
(d) Put open todos first and done ones last, or sort by due date
(e) Add a summary line, e.g. "2 open, 1 done"
(f) Something else, such as colour or different wording for the add/complete/error messages
If you're not sure, I'd suggest (a) + (b) + (c), with the done/error messages left as they are.

